## Project structure

```
~/CareerOS/
├── careeros/
│   ├── cli.py             Typer entry point
│   ├── config.py          Paths and .env loading
│   ├── db.py              SQLite schema and connection helpers
│   ├── facts.py           Immutable facts loader
│   ├── companies.py       Target companies loader
│   ├── notion_sync.py     One-way Bank sync from Notion (Notion → local)
│   ├── notion_apps.py     One-way Applications push to Notion (local → Notion, opposite direction)
│   ├── vet.py             Interactive vetting flow
│   ├── scan.py            Job fetch orchestrator
│   ├── jobs.py            Job triage (list, view, status, clear)
│   ├── intake.py          Manual job intake (URL or pasted JD) + geo_eligible()
│   ├── coach.py           Gap analysis: match Bank tech/tools against a job
│   ├── tailor.py          Tailoring package generator + budget check
│   ├── resume.py          DOCX resume builder (writes drafted content into a template)
│   ├── cover_letter.py    DOCX cover letter builder (same pattern, simpler template)
│   └── fetchers/
│       ├── base.py        Role keyword filter (positive + negative lists) + geo_eligible()
│       ├── greenhouse.py
│       ├── lever.py
│       └── ashby.py
├── data/
│   ├── facts.yaml               Immutable personal / education / employer / cert data (gitignored)
│   ├── facts.example.yaml       Template -- copy to facts.yaml
│   ├── companies.yaml           Target companies with ATS assignments (gitignored)
│   ├── companies.example.yaml   Template -- copy to companies.yaml
│   ├── resume_rules.md          Resume-tailoring session rules, read before editing your resume
│   ├── cover_letter_rules.md    Cover-letter session rules
│   └── careeros.db              SQLite (gitignored)
├── tests/                 pytest suite
├── logs/                  scan.log / scan.error.log if you set up scheduled scanning
├── applications/          Phase 4 output destination (gitignored)
├── .env                   NOTION_TOKEN and data source IDs (gitignored)
├── .env.example
├── pyproject.toml
├── CLAUDE.md               your personal instance (gitignored)
└── CLAUDE.md.example       this file
```

---

## Guardrails and gotchas

- **Never write to Notion without explicit approval.** The connection has update permission;
  the constraint is behavioral. When you say "approved" for a batch of proposed changes,
  that's the trigger.
- **Never invent metrics, tools, or claims** when helping with the Bank or resume tailoring.
  If a claim isn't grounded in your notes, Bullet Standard, or Metrics, ask, don't fill.
- **Never surface records tagged `Never Claim`** in any generated resume or cover letter,
  period -- define this tag (or your own equivalent) in your Notion Bank for anything you
  don't want to risk being asked about.
- **Preserve local enrichment columns on sync.** The sync module handles this; don't change
  that behavior without discussion.
- **Preserve user status on scan.** Same.
- **Role keyword filter lives in `careeros/fetchers/base.py`.** Edit `ROLE_KEYWORDS` and
  `NEGATIVE_KEYWORDS` there to include or exclude role types. Document *why* a keyword is
  excluded (e.g. a title that means something different at one company than another) so a
  future session doesn't second-guess it without context.
- **Geo eligibility filter lives in the same file** (`geo_eligible()`). It works off the
  *resolved* location (after falling back to parsing the JD body when the ATS field is
  vague), plus a narrow regex for explicit residency/timezone restriction phrases in the JD
  body. Broad region tags (e.g. an ATS's "AMER" label) are treated as open to your location
  by default -- if that's wrong for you (e.g. you're outside the US and "AMER" postings turn
  out to be US-only in practice), tighten it and re-check your existing backlog against the
  fix, the same way you'd re-check after any filter change.
- **ATS coverage is imperfect.** Companies with no public ATS API (Workday, custom systems,
  etc.) are marked `ats_type: unsupported`. Scan skips them and prints their careers URL for
  manual check. Building a Workday fetcher is a real rabbit hole; think twice before starting.
- **Tests run without network.** Fetcher tests use `httpx.MockTransport`. Real ATS calls
  happen only when running `careeros scan`.
- **Notion API version.** Uses `notion-client>=2.2.1`, which uses `data_sources.query()` (not
  the deprecated `databases.query()`). If the library changes again, this is where breakage
  would surface first.

---

## Ideas for extending this

- **Coach v2, if the grounded-only approach (decision #7) proves too narrow in practice.**
  Options to revisit deliberately, not by default: a curated skills dictionary for your
  target role type (accepts fabrication risk for broader coverage), or a Claude Code handoff
  package (JD + matched/unmatched records) for a human+AI judgment pass, mirroring the Model
  B2 pattern.
- **Scheduled scanning.** A macOS `launchd` LaunchAgent works for a "runs while my laptop is
  on" setup; a cloud-hosted agent with the DB made cloud-accessible (git-synced or hosted)
  would be needed for "runs even when my laptop is off," which is a bigger lift.
- **Desktop notifications on scan completion** via `osascript` if you want a heartbeat that
  the pipeline ran, independent of whether it found anything new.

Whatever you build, keep a decision log in the "Current status" section above -- the value
of this file compounds as it accumulates the *why* behind non-obvious choices, not just the
*what*.
